1.3. Patient Privacy Training. The Institution shall provide Students with compliance training in the applicable federal and state laws regarding the use and disclosure of protected health information, including the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (" HIPAA "), and rules and regulations promulgated therein.
16.3. HIPAA. If applicable, the Institution shall direct Students to comply with regulations governing the use and disclosure of protected health information under federal law, specifically HIPAA. In addition, the Institution hereby agreed to the following:
a. The Institution agrees to provide any training necessary to orient Students to HIPAA, their role in protecting PHI and their responsibility to comply with Exos’s policies and procedures regarding use and disclosure of PHI. Exos will provide awareness training for PHI, personally identifiable information and security essentials;
b. The Institution agrees that it is not a business associate (“ BA ”) of Exos, as defined within HIPAA, and Exos is not a BA of the Institution;
c. The Institution agrees that each Student has no rights to use PHI other than for legitimate, authorized, and legal purposes in their role as Student under the guidance of his/her supervisor; and
d. The Institution agrees each Student is subject to applicable policies and procedures of Exos.
